A||N||34||Monkeyman||Wing options||||5||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||11-05-2000||08:00 AM||||What are some non-stock wing options?  I like a large, thick look, not along the lines of the Firebird style.  Any suggestions?||||reg||5
Z||000001||MrPBody||11-05-2000||08:23 AM||||I'm going to try to adapt one from a Dodge Daytona.  It'll take some work, but it looks like it might fit.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||11-05-2000||08:37 AM||||After going to the bone yard this week. Spyro86SE and I took a Dodge Duster wing and put it on a Fiero. (Like the one in the pic of the yellow Fiero that gets posted here now & then) I gotta say that it fits perfect. And it looks real good for a non Fiero wing. <P><BR>Also Bam Bam has a 99/00 Mustang GT wing. For 2001 Ford changed it to this   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mustang1.jpg">  <BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/ny/jan21d2/images/mycar/back1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/ny/jan21d2/images/mycar/back1.jpg</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/ny/jan21d2/images/mycar/back2.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/ny/jan21d2/images/mycar/back2.jpg</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/ny/jan21d2/images/mycar/back3.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/ny/jan21d2/images/mycar/back3.jpg</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/ny/jan21d2/images/mycar/backside2.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/ny/jan21d2/images/mycar/backside2.jpg</A> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 11-05-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000003||Monkeyman||11-05-2000||08:40 AM||||I'm very mechanically challenged so I don't want anything that I have to work on.  I don't mind (yes, I do) drilling some holes in a fresh decklid, but that's about as far as I want to go.  I like the wing on (can't remember who--red, with white stripes)...but it looks a little narrower than I want.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||11-05-2000||02:20 PM||||I like the Duster wing, too. That same wing came on the Shadow ES and many of the other Shadow/Sundance derivatives. <BR>If you want a stock-looking but more reasonably priced wing, A&A makes a really nice knockoff. <A HREF="http://www.a-aspec.com/media/2712.GIF" TARGET=_blank>http://www.a-aspec.com/media/2712.GIF</A> <BR>The supports are molded into the bottom of the wing. The mounting holes are slightly different, though. <BR>If you want an IMSA spoiler, try RS motorsports. <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/fiero_catalog.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/fiero_catalog.htm</A> <P>Raydar<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||TheFiero64||11-05-2000||04:51 PM||||I have the AA wing on my 88. I got it for $150. I have had many complements on it. The stands are molded into the wing itself. Here is a Pic I took in the rain.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/luckyplugs.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000006||BroCar 87||11-05-2000||05:14 PM||||Hey guys, I like the low profile look on the coupes. The high wings (as said earlier in the month) look more 80's style. Look at todays cars, no spoiler or low spoiler. If I were to get a spoiler on my fiero, which I want to do anyways, I would get the NEW Grand Am spoiler.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grandamspoiler.jpg">   They are very unique. <P>There is my two cents, so there!!!! hehe!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature2.jpg">  <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>   Custom dual side exit exhaust!||||reg||6
Z||000007||Cooter||11-05-2000||05:26 PM||||how about this one: <A HREF="http://www.a-aspec.com/media/gtr_wing.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.a-aspec.com/media/gtr_wing.jpg</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||rockcrawl||11-05-2000||05:29 PM||||Here's a picture of a custom style wing from A&A Specialties. It's very similar to an OEM wing but the tips extend forward almost to the base of the notchback, and the pedastals are built in. It won't fit a fastback. A&A part# 1355. A friend of mine owns this car now, so if you want more (better) pics, let me know.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86peg_1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT (awaiting new engine)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<P>"Confidence is the feeling you have before you fully understand the situation"<p>[This message has been edited by rockcrawl (edited 11-05-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000009||Phil||11-05-2000||06:22 PM||||If you mean this one- it's just a stock wing on 7 1/2" stands<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wing_2.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by Phil (edited 11-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Philphine||11-05-2000||06:34 PM||||check wings for late '80s, early '90s mustang coupe/conv. look in a copy of muscle mustangs and fast fords mag. also iroc z wings and fire bird factory and after market wings sit on the rear and look pretty good demensionaly. also recently saw a fiero wing on a late model t-bird that looked pretty good so the opposite may be true too.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Raydar||11-05-2000||06:57 PM||||Here's the A&A IROC spoiler.  <A HREF="http://www.a-aspec.com/media/2724.GIF" TARGET=_blank>http://www.a-aspec.com/media/2724.GIF</A> <BR>Had one on my Firebird. Thought it really matched the lines of the car. Was thinking about trying it on the Fiero, but sold the Firebird before I got a chance. <BR>If you're going to try one on your Fiero, it may not fit correctly on the ends. See if you can find one to try before you buy.<P>Raydar ||||reg||1
