Z||000014||BAM-BAM||11-05-2000||08:22 PM||||  Monk, My 2000 Mustang spoiler was a sinch to install all the directions are on Haze's website. It works well on the notchback, not to sure it would fly on the fastback. On the notch back it pulls that line just aft of the rear wheels and really sweetn's the body flow. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/leftside85gt.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rearview85gt_1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rightside85gt_1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tightviewspoiler_1.jpg"> <P>  All the info you need is on Haze's site, but don't be afraid to E-Mail me at bartlettds@lvcm.com   or you can call (702)-243-3744 <P> Peace, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Guages And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||6
