Z||000018||Raydar||11-06-2000||09:22 AM||||All the IMSA spoilers I've seen (there are two designs for the notchback) are mounted by drilling holes down each side of the decklid. They can be bonded/glassed in, if you want. I've seen them done both ways.<BR>The IRM piece (2nd design) might be an inch or so wider than the RS Motorsports piece. Not sure, though. It covers the entire back of the decklid, and has a hole drilled for access to the lock. The RSM piece only comes down to the middle of the lock cylinder. AFAIK, this was the first design. <BR>I was unhappy with the quality of IRM's piece. If I order another one, I'm going to  try RSM's. (Just beginning a project. Not sure how it's gonna end up, yet.)<BR>If you want some "up close" pics of the IRM piece, let me know.  <P>Raydar||||reg||1
Z||000019||BAM-BAM||11-06-2000||10:36 AM||||   Monk, How about something like this?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/803.jpg"> <P>   <A HREF="http://www.stangparts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.stangparts.com</A> <P>  Late, BAM OUT!<P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Guages And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||12
