Z||000023||Philphine||11-07-2000||02:27 AM||||you know me. i'm pic challenged. try this, measure the rear edge of a coupe/conv. mustang. then measure the width of the trunk lid. move up about 12" and take the same measurements. take the same measurements on your fiero. you'll be surprised how close they are. the only real difference is the mustang rear slopes downward a little more. i thought that might be a problem but it still looks good. plus i've heard off and on that most passenger car wings have little or no effect on aerodymamics do the few degrees difference might make it slightly functional. <P>at best i could take some shots and snail 'em to you.||||reg||1
Z||000024||Raydar||11-07-2000||10:57 AM||||Wha..? Who...? Ummmmm... Okay. <BR>I'm awake now.<BR>I'll take pics and post 'em. Probably won't be tonight, though. By the time I get home, it'll be dark. Gotta cast my vote, ya' know!<P>Raydar||||reg||1
Z||000025||Monkeyman||11-07-2000||06:22 PM||||The more I look at a whale tail/IMSA wing, the more I like 'em.  There's nothing wrong with a smaller wing, but that gives the impression of refinement.  The fastback might look refined, but the notchback just looks strong and mean.  Gotta have a huge wing (but not a ricer wing--there's a difference).  Send some pics, either through email or snail mail.  ||||reg||1
